sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant U as User wallet
    participant MP as Public mempool
    participant S as Searcher
    participant B as Block builder
    participant P as WETH/USDC pool<br/>1,000 / 4,000,000
    participant A as Arbitrageur

    U->>U: Quote 10 WETH -> 39,486.32 USDC<br/>set amountOutMin = 39,091.46 (1% tolerance)
    U->>MP: Broadcast swapExactTokensForTokens
    MP->>S: Transaction visible with its minOut
    S->>S: Solve for the largest front-run that still<br/>leaves the victim above minOut: 5.07 WETH

    Note over S,B: One atomic bundle, three transactions
    S->>B: tx1 sell 5.07 WETH, tx2 = victim, tx3 buy back
    B->>B: Place the bundle at the top of the block<br/>in exchange for a priority payment
    B->>P: tx1 executes, reserves 1,005.07 / 3,979,882.53
    B->>P: tx2 executes, victim receives 39,091.49 USDC<br/>exactly 1.000% worse than quoted
    B->>P: tx3 executes, searcher buys back 5.1402 WETH

    Note over S: Searcher profit 0.0702 WETH, about $281<br/>Victim loss $394.83<br/>LPs keep $114.20 in extra fees

    P->>A: Pool price now off-market again
    A->>P: Arbitrage back to 4,000
    Note over U,A: Nothing here is a bug. Every step<br/>is the contract behaving exactly as written.
